meta {
  name: Health check
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/up
  body: none
  auth: none
}

tests {
  test("the app booted", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Rails' own health endpoint. Run this first: every other failure in this
  collection is easier to read once you know the stack is up.

  `/up` is also a reserved path (config/initializers/reserved_paths.rb), so it
  is the one case where a three-character path is *not* treated as a short code
  — see `03 - Redirect / Reserved path is not a code`.
}
